  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 18,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.087,
            0.888,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Place 1 coin in the left pan (call it effort) and 1 identical coin in the right pan (call it load). Observe that the beam stays horizontal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.125,
            0.89,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Add one more coin to the right pan, so that it contains 2 coins. The beam tilts. Move the heavier pan closer to the centre of the beam to balance the beam. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measure",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " its distance from the centre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.18,
            0.888,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Repeat step 5 with 4 coins and then 8 coins in the right pan. Each time, note its distance from the centre that balances the beam."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.217,
            0.888,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Record",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " all observations and measurements, and complete the Table 7.1 by adding more rows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.284,
            0.886,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.223,
                0.263,
                0.828,
                0.28
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 7.1: Number of coins in the left pan and its distance from the fulcrum"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.227,
                0.284,
                0.886,
                0.422
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_table_5.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>Number of Coinsin left pan,<eq>n _ { 1 }</eq>(Effort)</td><td>Distance of leftpan from thefulcrum,<eq>L _ { 1 }</eq>(cm)</td><td>Number of coinsin right pan,<eq>n _ { 2 }</eq>(Load)</td><td>Distance of rightpan from thefulcrum,<eq>L _ { 2 }</eq>(cm)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td></td><td>1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td></td><td>2</td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.439,
            0.888,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By analysing the values recoded in Table 7.1, you can "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "conclude",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that the beam balances when"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.474,
            0.625,
            0.493
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "n_{1} \\times L_{1}^{*} = n_{2} \\times L_{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.494,
            0.259,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Or,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.376,
            0.494,
            0.887,
            0.512
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{effort} \\times \\mathrm{effort} \\; \\mathrm{arm} = \\mathrm{load} \\times \\mathrm{l} \\; \\mathrm{load} \\; \\mathrm{arm}\\tag{7.15}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.514,
            0.888,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the effort arm is increased, the effort required to move the same load is reduced. You can calculate the mechanical advantage of the lever by using Eq. (7.12). Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.565,
            0.887,
            0.602
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{mechanism\\_advantage} = \\frac{\\mathrm{load}}{\\mathrm{effort}} = \\frac{\\mathrm{effort\\ arm}}{\\mathrm{load\\ arm}}\\tag{7.16}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.602,
            0.889,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, by increasing the effort arm, the lever applies a larger force "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the load than the effort "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F_{1}^{\\cdot}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The lever thus allows us to gain a mechanical advantage equal to the ratio of the distances, i.e., "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { L _ { 1 } } { L _ { 2 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.675,
            0.89,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "With the use of a lever, the effort required is generally smaller but it has to move by a larger distance such that the total work done by the agency applying effort remains the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
            0.741,
            0.305,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.082,
                0.741,
                0.305,
                0.894
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.126,
                0.898,
                0.265,
                0.913
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.34: A seesaw"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.73,
            0.89,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7.13:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " For a seesaw having four seats A, B, D, E and fulcrum at C (Fig. 7.34), AC = EC = 2 m and BC = DC = 1 m. On which seats should children of masses 15 kg and 30 kg sit to make the seesaw balanced?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.801,
            0.89,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Suppose the child of mass 15 kg sits on seat A and the other child sits at a distance L from the fulcrum. Using Eq. (7.15), we obtain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.855,
            0.555,
            0.874
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "15\\; kg  \\times 2\\; m  = 30\\; kg  \\times L"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.876,
            0.423,
            0.893
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "L = 1   \\mathrm { m }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.896,
            0.684,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the other child should sit at seat D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.943,
            0.115,
            0.96
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "134"
            }
          ]
        },
